95,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $A \\land (C \\lor B)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\land C) \\lor (A \\land B)$","choice2":"$(A \\lor C) \\land (A \\lor B)$","choice3":"$A \\lor (B \\land C)$","choice4":"$(A \\land C) \\land (A \\land B)$","choice5":"$(A \\lor C) \\lor (A \\lor B)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nA \\land (C \\lor B) \\equiv (A \\land C) \\lor (A \\land B)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403224,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:48:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12875},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403235,"created":"2026-10-16T19:48:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13612,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:48 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":128636,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $X \\land (Q \\lor \\neg Z)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$ (Q \\land X) \\lor (\\neg Z \\land X)$","choice2":"$\\neg Z \\land (X \\lor Q)$","choice3":"$ (Q \\land X) \\land (\\neg Z \\land X)$","choice4":"$X \\lor (Q \\land \\neg Z)$","choice5":"$(\\neg Z \\land Q) \\lor (\\neg Z \\land X)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nX \\land (Q \\lor \\neg Z) \\equiv (X \\land Q) \\lor (X \\land \\neg Z)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $X \\land Q \\equiv Q \\land X$ and $X \\land \\neg Z \\equiv \\neg Z \\land X,$ we can write</p>\n<p>\\[\n(X \\land Q) \\lor (X \\land \\neg Z) \\equiv (Q \\land X) \\lor (\\neg Z \\land X).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403235,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:48:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13612},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403248,"created":"2026-10-16T19:48:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10895,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:48 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":81596,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7077,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\lor B) \\land C?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land C)$","choice2":"$(A \\land B) \\lor C$","choice3":"$(A \\land C) \\land (B \\land C)$","choice4":"$A \\land (B \\lor C)$","choice5":"$(A \\lor C) \\lor (B \\lor C)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(A \\lor B) \\land C \\equiv (A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land C)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7077,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Conjunction"},"group":{"id":15102,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403248,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:48:36.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10895},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403260,"created":"2026-10-16T19:48:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11200,"number":5,"c