conjunction, as follows:\n\\[\n(X \\land \\neg Y) \\lor Z \\equiv (X  \\lor  Z)  \\land ( \\neg Y  \\lor  Z)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403274,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:49:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12517},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403285,"created":"2026-10-16T19:49:31.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":16295,"number":7,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:49 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":81610,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg P \\land Q) \\lor R?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\land (R \\lor Q)$","choice2":"$(R \\lor P) \\land (\\neg Q \\lor R)$","choice3":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\lor (R \\lor P)$","choice4":"$(R \\lor \\neg P) \\land Q$","choice5":"$\\neg P \\land (R \\lor Q)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg P \\land Q) \\lor R \\equiv (\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (Q \\lor R)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, since $\\neg P \\lor R \\equiv R \\lor \\neg P$ and $Q \\lor R \\equiv R \\lor Q$ we can write\n\\[\n(\\neg P \\lor R) \\land (Q \\lor R) \\equiv (R \\lor \\neg P) \\land (R \\lor Q).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403285,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:49:31.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeRespons