rmat":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $P\\lor (\\neg Q \\land \\neg R)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(P \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (P \\lor \\neg R)$","choice2":"$P \\land (\\neg R \\lor \\neg Q)$","choice3":"$(P \\lor \\neg Q) \\lor (P \\lor \\neg R)$","choice4":"$(P \\land \\neg Q) \\lor (P \\land \\neg R)$","choice5":"$(P \\land \\neg Q) \\land (P \\land \\neg R)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nP\\lor (\\neg Q \\land \\neg R) \\equiv (P \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (P \\lor \\neg R)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403303,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:50:07.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12969},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403311,"created":"2026-10-16T19:50:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12475,"number":10,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:50 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":81078,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7124,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $Z \\lor (X \\land Y)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(Z \\lor X) \\land (Z \\lor Y)$","choice2":" $(Z \\land X) \\lor (Z \\land Y)$","choice3":"$Z \\land (X \\lor Y)$","choice4":" $(Z \\lor X) \\land Y$","choice5":" $(Z \\lor X) \\lor (Z \\lor Y)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nZ \\lor (X \\land Y) \\equiv (Z \\lor X) \\land (Z \\lor Y)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7124,"title":"Expanding a Statement by Distributing a Disjunction"},"group":{"id":15104,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403311,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:50:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12475},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7078,"number":3,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions","answers":[{"id":62403325,"created":"2026-10-16T19:50:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13909,"number":11,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:50 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":81079,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(H \\land K) \\lor (L \\land K)?$</p>\n","choice1":" $(H \\lor L) \\land K$","choice2":" $(H \\land L) \\lor K$","choice3":" $(H \\lor K) \\land L$","choice4":"$K \\land (H \\land L)$","choice5":"  $(H \\lor L) \\lor K$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $K,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(H \\land K) \\lor (L \\land K) \\equiv (H \\lor L) \\land K\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403325,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:50:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13909},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403336,"created":"2026-10-16T19:51:03.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12240,"number":12,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:51 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":86773,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg L \\land H) \\lor (K \\land H)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$H \\land (\\neg L \\lor K)$","choice2":"$\\neg H \\land (L \\lor K)$","choice3":"$H \\land ( L \\land K)$","choice4":"$H \\lor (\\neg L \\lor \\neg K)$","choice5":"$( L \\lor K) \\land H$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $H,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg L \\land H) \\lor (K \\land H) \\equiv (\\neg L \\lor K) \\land H\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can write\n\\[\n(\\neg L \\lor K) \\land H \\equiv H \\land (\\neg L \\lor K).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403336,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:51:03.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12240},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403347,"created":"2026-10-16T19:51:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14551,"number":13,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:51 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":86771,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(M \\land \\neg N) \\lor (M \\land \\neg R)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$M \\land (\\neg N \\lor \\neg R)$","choice2":"$M \\land (\\neg N \\land  R)$","choice3":"$\\neg M \\land (N \\lor R)$","choice4":"$M \\lor (\\neg N \\land \\neg R)$","choice5":"$\\neg M \\lor (N \\land R)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>We can factor out the conjunction with $M,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(M \\land \\neg N) \\lor (M \\land \\neg R) \\equiv M \\land (\\neg N \\lor \\neg R)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403347,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:51:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14551},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403362,"created":"2026-10-16T19:51:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":18341,"number":14,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:51 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:18","question":{"id":81615,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg A \\land B) \\lor (\\neg A \\land C)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\neg A \\land (C \\lor B)$","choice2":"$(\\neg A \\land C) \\lor B$","choice3":"$\\neg A \\lor  (C \\lor B)$","choice4":"$\\neg A \\land (C \\land B)$","choice5":"$\\neg B \\land (C \\lor A)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $\\neg A,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg A \\land B) \\lor (\\neg A \\land C) \\equiv \\neg A \\land (B \\lor C)\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, since $B \\lor C \\equiv C \\lor B,$ we can write\n\\[\n\\neg A \\land (B \\lor C) \\equiv \\neg A \\land (C \\lor B).\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403362,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:51:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":18341},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403371,"created":"2026-10-16T19:52:08.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17159,"number":15,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:52 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":128646,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7078,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land C)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(B \\lor A) \\land C$","choice2":"$B \\lor  (A \\land C)$","choice3":"$(B \\lor A)  \\lor C$","choice4":"$(B \\land A) \\land C$","choice5":"$B  \\land (A \\lor C)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we can factor out the conjunction with $C,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(A \\land C) \\lor (B \\land C) \\equiv (A \\lor B) \\land C\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, since $A \\lor B \\equiv B \\lor A,$ we can write\n\\[\n(A \\lor B) \\land C \\equiv (B \\lor A) \\land C.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7078,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Conjunctions"},"group":{"id":15103,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403371,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:52:08.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17159},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":7125,"number":4,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions","answers":[{"id":62403381,"created":"2026-10-16T19:52:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14506,"number":16,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:52 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":86774,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(\\neg M \\lor K) \\land (\\neg M \\lor L)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\neg M \\lor (K \\land L)$","choice2":"$M \\lor (\\neg K \\land \\neg L)$","choice3":"$\\neg M \\land (K \\lor L)$","choice4":"$\\neg M \\lor (K \\lor L)$","choice5":"$\\neg M \\land (K \\land L)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We can factor out the disjunction with $\\neg M,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(\\neg M \\lor K) \\land (\\neg M \\lor L) \\equiv \\neg M \\lor (K \\land L)\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403381,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:52:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14506},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62403390,"created":"2026-10-16T19:52:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13136,"number":17,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 7:52 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81617,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7125,"text":"<p>Which statement is equivalent to $(X \\lor Y) \\land (Z \\lor Y)?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(X \\land Z) \\lor Y$","choice2":"$(X \\land Y) \\lor Z$","choice3":"$(X \\lor Z) \\land Y$","choice4":"$Y \\land (X \\land Z) $","choice5":"$Y \\lor (X \\lor Z) $","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>We can factor out the disjunction with $Y,$ as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(X \\lor Y) \\land (Z \\lor Y) \\equiv (X \\land Z) \\lor Y\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2822,"name":"The Distributive Laws"},"example":{"id":7125,"title":"Simplifying a Statement Using the Distributive Property for Disjunctions"},"group":{"id":15105,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272819,"answer":{"id":62403390,"cread":"2026-10-16T19:52:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13136